        "hero_title": "Small Things. \nBig Buzz.",
        "story_image": "shopify://shop_images/ourstory.jpg",
        "story_content": "<h3>It started with a stall (and a sister who had enough of my nonsense)</h3><p>Picture this: a crowded stall, fairy lights, a table full of beautiful jewelry, and me, standing next to it with nothing to sell. Just vibes. Moral support. Occasionally holding things.</p><p>My sister was the one with the brand. I was the one who tagged along to help set up, then stood around while she did the actual work.</p><p>Until one day she looked at me and said, \"Why are you just coming along and doing nothing? You should sell something too. Be productive.\"</p><p>Rude? A little. Fair? Completely.</p><h3>The first little experiments</h3><p>So, I did. I started small, with the things I loved: posters that made a wall feel like a personality, stickers you'd slap on a laptop without thinking twice, bookmarks for people who read (or want to look like they do), and a few little keychains.</p><p>No grand plan. No business course. Just a table, a handful of products, and a lot of curiosity about whether anyone else would love this stuff as much as I did.</p><p>They did. Then the buzz began!!!</p><p>People stopped. They picked things up. They smiled. They came back with friends. Someone bought a keychain for themselves, then came back for three more as gifts.</p><p>That's when it clicked: the little things people carry, stick, hang, and gift are never really \"little.\" They're the things that make a day, a bag, a desk, or a wall feel like yours.</p><p>So Buzzko was born. The name says it all: that spark of excitement you feel when you find something you didn't know you needed.</p><h3>From keychains to a whole universe</h3><p>What began with four products has grown, one obsession at a time: charms, crochet pieces, lighters and plenty more trending finds that make us go \"okay, we need this.\"</p><p>Some of it is quirky. Some are cute. Some are a little chaotic. All of it has one thing in common: I only sell what I'm genuinely passionate about. If I wouldn't buy it, gift it, or proudly display it, it doesn't make the cut. No filler, no \"this will probably sell.\" Just stuff with personality.</p><h3>Yes, there's an engineer behind this!!!</h3><p>Here's the plot twist: I'm an engineer by profession. My days are about logic, systems, and things that must work properly.</p><p>Buzzko is my other side. It's where I get to be creative, playful, and a little unpredictable. It's the side hustle that doesn't feel like work, built in the margins of a busy life: evenings, weekends, and every bit of spare energy I have.</p><p>That means Buzzko is built bit by bit, and I'm proud of that. Every order, every restock, every new product has been grown with care, not rushed out by a corporation. Behind every package is a real person who is genuinely excited that you picked it.</p><h3>What we believe</h3><p>Everyday things shouldn't be boring. Your keys, your bag, your desk, your walls: all of them deserve some personality.</p><p>Passion beats trends. We follow what's hot, but only if we love it too.</p><p>Small brands have big hearts. Every purchase supports a dream being built from scratch.</p><p>Fun is a feature, not a bonus. If it doesn't make you smile, we're not interested.</p><p>Every brand has a few people working quietly in the background, and mine has one who deserves a spotlight, even if she prefers to stay in the shadows.</p><p>She helped me turn Buzzko from a table full of products into an actual website you can visit, scroll, and shop from. She believed in this idea when it was still small, backed me when I was juggling a day job and a side hustle, and gave her time and energy without being asked twice.</p><p>She knows who she is. Her support has shaped Buzzko more than she probably realizes, and every order that comes through this site exists partly because of her.</p><p>Thank you. This brand has your fingerprints on it. 💛</p><h3>Thank you to my customers!!!</h3><p>Every person who has bought, shared, gifted, or just cheered us on has helped this tiny idea grow. You're the reason a stall-side side-quest turned into a brand.</p><p>And to my sister, who told me to stop standing around and start selling, Thank you. This is all your fault. 🙂</p><p>So, scroll around, find something that makes you grin, and take a little piece of Buzzko home.</p><p><strong>Stay curious. Stay quirky. Stay Buzzing. 🐝</strong></p>",
